<title>SPAIN: Spain approves 3 pct cut in electricity rates.</title>
<headline>Spain approves 3 pct cut in electricity rates.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government on Friday approved a cut in electricity tariffs by an average of three percent from January 1, Industry Minister Josep Pique said.</p>
<p>&quot;The reduction for the next year is an average of three percent in nominal terms...This means in real term we are approaching a reduction of around six percent,&quot; Pique said.</p>
<p>The convervative government has said it plans to reduce tariffs by eight percent in the next five years.</p>
</text>
